{
  "info": {
    "name": "Applicant Service",
    "description": "Applicant Service - Team 17 \"Student ID, please\".\n\nOwns an applicant's claimed identity. Covers the full CRUD, every error path, and the shift check against Server Moderation Session Service (a shift that does not exist is 404, one that has not started is 409).\n\nEvery response is checked for the absence of `deception`: it is the answer to the puzzle the players solve, so leaking it would end the game.\n\nRun the service first - see docker-compose.yml. Requests are ordered to run start to finish: the first three open a real shift, and creating an applicant stores its id for the requests that follow.\n\nLab 3: the two round-robin requests show the Gateway alternating between the two replicas - each response names the replica that answered in X-Instance-Id.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Every request goes through the Gateway, which only lets a request in with a valid Bearer token.",
          "// The first request of a run registers a throwaway player and logs in; the token is reused by the",
          "// requests after it and renewed after 50 minutes, since Player Service issues it for one hour.",
          "const obtainedAt = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('token_obtained_at') || 0);",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('token') || Date.now() - obtainedAt > 50 * 60 * 1000) {",
          "  const baseUrl = pm.variables.get('base_url');",
          "  const suffix = Date.now();",
          "  const player = { username: `pairtwo${suffix}`, email: `pairtwo${suffix}@example.com`, password: 'secret123' };",
          "  const post = (path, body) => ({",
          "    url: baseUrl + path,",
          "    method: 'POST',",
          "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
          "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(body) },",
          "  });",
          "  pm.sendRequest(post('/players', player), (registerError) => {",
          "    if (registerError) throw registerError;",
          "    pm.sendRequest(post('/players/login', { email: player.email, password: player.password }), (loginError, response) => {",
          "      if (loginError) throw loginError;",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set('token', response.json().token);",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set('token_obtained_at', String(Date.now()));",
          "    });",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Shift - open one (Server Moderation Session Service)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/sessions",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "sessions"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lab 3. Applicant Service asks Server Moderation Session Service over gRPC whether a shift is running before an applicant joins it, so the run opens a real shift first. The player this collection logged in becomes its Moderator."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('the shift is open but not started', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('created'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('session_id', body.session_id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
